meta {
  name: 03 Malformed Patient ID
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/chat
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cookie: copilot_session={{copilot_session}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "message": "Give me a quick orientation on this patient: active problems, current meds, and allergies.",
    "patient_id": "not-a-real-patient-id-1234"
  }
}

docs {
  Auth: requires the copilot_session environment variable to be set to a real,
  still-valid session cookie -- see bruno/README.md. Without it this 401s with
  {"detail": "Not logged in..."} regardless of the scenario below.

  A patient_id that does not correspond to any real FHIR resource.

  Look for in the response:
  - A graceful failure -- the tool call returns "not found" (or similar)
    and the model reports that back honestly, rather than fabricating a
    patient chart or crashing the request.
  - No 500 error at the HTTP layer; the /chat endpoint itself should still
    return 200 with a response body describing the lookup failure.
}
